From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: UniqueJar <mihaifica34@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 23:02:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] UniqueJar: Cache synched health in a field for isAlive()

ActivationRange.checkIfActive() calls isAlive() for every ticking entity
every tick. isAlive() read health through SynchedEntityData
(entity -> itemsById[] -> DataItem -> boxed Float): ~3.5% of server-thread
CPU samples in the baseline workload.

LivingEntity now mirrors DATA_HEALTH_ID in a primitive float, updated at the
only three places that write DATA_HEALTH_ID. ServerPlayer keeps the original
formula because getHealth() returns Bukkit's unscaled health there.
With -ea, isAlive() asserts the mirror equals the synched value.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/net/minecraft/server/level/ServerPlayer.java b/net/minecraft/server/level/ServerPlayer.java
index 4030776c3d12f8e797720180e141322b5d2cc548..3a58a3576659901c31eb1405c82391fa10f87391 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/server/level/ServerPlayer.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/server/level/ServerPlayer.java
@@ -1183,6 +1183,14 @@ public class ServerPlayer extends Player implements ca.spottedleaf.moonrise.patc
         }
     }
     // Paper end - Expand PlayerDeathEvent API
+
+    // UniqueJar start - Cache synched health in a field for isAlive()
+    @Override
+    public boolean isAlive() {
+        return !this.dead && !this.isRemoved() && this.getHealth() > 0.0F; // getHealth() reads Bukkit's unscaled health, not the synched field
+    }
+    // UniqueJar end - Cache synched health in a field for isAlive()
+
     @Override
     public void die(final DamageSource source) {
         // this.gameEvent(GameEvent.ENTITY_DIE); // Paper - move below event cancellation check
